meta {
  name: 6. Add Bank Account
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/bank-accounts/verify
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "accountNumber": "{{bankAccountNumber}}",
    "ifscCode": "{{bankIfscCode}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Adds and verifies a bank account in one call. Beneficiary name is taken from the driver's own
  profile, not the request — there's no beneficiaryName field to fill in.

  On a name mismatch against the verification provider, the account comes back with
  status AWAITING_ID_PROOF instead of VERIFIED. Resolving that (PUT
  /api/bank-accounts/{id}/id-proof) is a separate, less-common path — see the reference
  collection, not part of this happy-path flow.

  Either this step or step 7 (UPI) is enough to satisfy "at least one payout method" — both
  are shown here so you can see both paths, not because both are required.
}
